BF16 Tensor-Core QSA indexer scores (fn_qsa_scores_tc / fn_qsa_scores_tc_paged)

Replaces the scalar FP32 FMA inner loop in `qsa_tile::scores` for prompt chunks
(rows >= 16, HI == 4, DI == 128) with BF16 `mma16816` Tensor Core instructions
using FP32 accumulators (same `qmm_frag::ldmatrix4` + `qmm_frag::mma` primitive
used by `fn_attn_chunks`), with both contiguous and paged variants.
Gated by `TF_FLASHNEXT_QSA_TC` (default 1; `0` restores scalar `qsa_tile::scores`).

Verified on GB10 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 4.05bpw + DFlash2):
- 248K cold prefill: 147.42 s (1,679.6 tok/s) -> 141.63 s (1,748.4 tok/s) (-5.8 s / +4.1% total)
- 65K cold prefill: 34.19 s (1,908.3 tok/s) -> 33.86 s (1,926.9 tok/s)
- Exactness: 120K needle retrieval byte-identical (sha ae38468a7f52, FALCON-9472-OMEGA),
  5/5 greedy and 5/5 T=0.7 token_sha256 identical to stock, drafts on == drafts off.

